---
import DefaultLayout from '../../layouts/DefaultLayout.astro';
---

<DefaultLayout
  title="Community"
  subtitle="Stay in touch with the Wicket community"
>

  <p>
    Apache Wicket has a large and active community with over twenty years of development and
    thousands of developers building great Wicket applications around the world. Here you can
    find how to get help, contribute, and stay connected.
  </p>

  <h2>Mailing Lists</h2>
  <p>
    The mailing lists are the primary way to ask questions and discuss Wicket. Many experienced
    Wicket developers are subscribed and ready to help.
  </p>

  <h3>Users List</h3>
  <p>
    Ask questions and help other users on the users list. Announcements and security updates are
    also sent to this list.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Address: <a href="mailto:users@wicket.apache.org">users@wicket.apache.org</a></li>
    <li>
      <a href="mailto:users-subscribe@wicket.apache.org?subject=Subscribe+to+Apache+Wicket+User+list">
        Subscribe
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://lists.apache.org/list.html?users@wicket.apache.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Browse archives
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Developers List</h3>
  <p>
    Discuss the internals of the framework, propose new features, and follow development
    activity. Low-traffic list.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Address: <a href="mailto:dev@wicket.apache.org">dev@wicket.apache.org</a></li>
    <li>
      <a href="mailto:dev-subscribe@wicket.apache.org?subject=Subscribe+to+Apache+Wicket+Dev+list">
        Subscribe
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://lists.apache.org/list.html?dev@wicket.apache.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Browse archives
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <h2>Chat</h2>
  <p>
    For more direct discussions, join the <strong>#wicket</strong> IRC channel on
    <a href="https://freenode.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Freenode</a>.
    Note that time zones can make it difficult to find activity at all hours.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <h2>Contributing</h2>
  <p>
    Want to help make Wicket better? There are many ways to contribute — from answering
    questions on the mailing list to submitting code patches.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/community/contributing">How to contribute to Apache Wicket</a></li>
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <h2>GitHub</h2>
  <p>
    The Apache Wicket source code is hosted on GitHub. You can browse the code, open issues,
    and submit pull requests.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://github.com/apache/wicket" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        github.com/apache/wicket
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <h2>WicketStuff</h2>
  <p>
    WicketStuff is an umbrella project gathering many community-provided sub-projects. These
    cover everything from integration with popular JavaScript frameworks (TinyMCE, Foundation,
    etc.) to advanced features like async task execution and RESTful applications.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://github.com/wicketstuff/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        github.com/wicketstuff
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://github.com/wicketstuff/core/wiki" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        WicketStuff sub-projects overview
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    If you have discovered a security vulnerability in Apache Wicket, please follow the
    Apache Software Foundation's responsible disclosure process.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://www.apache.org/security/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Apache Security Process
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Report via email: <a href="mailto:security@apache.org">security@apache.org</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <h2>Projects Built with Wicket</h2>
  <p>
    Curious about who else is using Wicket?
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/community/who-uses-wicket">Who Uses Wicket</a></li>
  </ul>

</DefaultLayout>
